The Forge — third-party material and what it requires
=====================================================

This repository is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). It also touches material owned by
others. Nothing third-party is vendored here as data: the catalogs are generated
from published standards, the external-dataset code is a *converter* and the
datasets themselves are never committed or fetched by the server. What follows is
the inventory anyway, because the obligations are real and the provenance fields
in the code exist so this list can be rebuilt rather than remembered.

Adafruit_CAD_Parts — MIT
  `backend/app/services/adafruit_parts.py` carries a manifest of 484 models
  pinned to a revision, verified against the git blob hash and downloaded on
  first placement. The models are Adafruit's and MIT licensed; the licence text
  ships beside the code at
  `backend/app/services/data/ADAFRUIT-LICENSE.txt`.

Zero-To-CAD-1m — Apache-2.0
  `backend/datasets/external.py` converts that dataset's CadQuery programs into
  this catalog's operation sequences. The converter is original work; the dataset
  is not redistributed here and is not downloaded by the server. Anyone using the
  converter against the dataset takes it under Apache-2.0, which requires the
  licence and attribution to travel with any copy of the *data*.

SketchGraphs / Onshape public documents — Onshape Terms of Use §1.g.ii
  The sketch converter rests on the grant in §1.g.ii, which gives anyone
  accessing a public Onshape document a licence to "use, copy, modify, merge,
  publish, distribute, sublicense" its contents. No Onshape data is committed.

Declined, and recorded so the reasons are not relitigated
  Fusion 360 Gallery is non-commercial-research only. 3Dfindit/CADENAS disallows
  this crawler in robots.txt and answers non-browser clients 403. TraceParts'
  terms forbid distributing its data "on any storage medium whatsoever", which no
  posture relaxes. BOLTS (GPL-3), the FreeCAD Fasteners workbench (GPL-2) and
  NopSCADlib (GPL-3) were used only as an independent cross-check on tables
  generated from the standards — **nothing was transcribed from them**, which is
  what leaves this repository distributable at all. See
  `docs/PURCHASED-PARTS-SOURCING.md`.

Standards
  ISO 4762, 4032, 7089, 2338, 273, 261, 2306, 68-1, 54, 286, ISO 15 and
  NEMA ICS 16 dimensions are facts stated in those standards. A dimension carries
  no licence; the standards documents themselves are copyrighted and are not
  reproduced here.
